@startuml AircraftManagement-SD-OwnerCommand
autonumber
title Command forwarded to the owner replica — PATCH /api/aircrafts/{registrationNumber}/status (US105, contract B3b)
actor "ATCC / Maintenance" as User
participant "aircraftmanagement-1\n: AircraftController" as Ctrl
participant ": UpdateAircraftStatusService" as Service
participant "aircraftRepo (H2 #1)" as Repo
participant ": PeerClient" as Peers
participant "aircraftmanagement-2\n(owner of CS-TUC)" as R2
participant "aircraftRepo (H2 #2)" as Repo2
participant "aircraftmanagement-3" as R3

activate User
User -> Ctrl : PATCH /api/aircrafts/CS-TUC/status\n{"status":"UNDER_MAINTENANCE"}
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Service : updateStatus("CS-TUC", dto)
activate Service
Service -> Service : AircraftStatus.parse(dto.status)\n(unknown → 400, before forwarding)
Service -> Repo : findById("CS-TUC")
Repo --> Service : empty (not stored here)

Service -> Peers : forwardToOwner(PATCH, "/api/aircrafts/CS-TUC/status", dto, AircraftDTO)
activate Peers
note right of Peers
  Unicast: peers are tried ONE AT A TIME.
  Same method, path, body and JWT; X-Peer-Hops: 1.
end note
Peers -> R3 : PATCH /api/aircrafts/CS-TUC/status
R3 -> R3 : hops=1 → no re-forwarding
R3 --> Peers : 404 (not mine) → try next peer
Peers -> R2 : PATCH /api/aircrafts/CS-TUC/status
activate R2
R2 -> Repo2 : findById("CS-TUC")
Repo2 --> R2 : Aircraft (version 5)
R2 -> R2 : aircraft.changeStatus(UNDER_MAINTENANCE)
R2 -> Repo2 : saveAndFlush(aircraft)
note right of Repo2
  @Version: UPDATE ... WHERE version = 5.
  A concurrent change already committed → 409.
end note
Repo2 --> R2 : Aircraft (version 6)
R2 --> Peers : 200 AircraftDTO (UNDER_MAINTENANCE)
deactivate R2
Peers --> Service : Optional(AircraftDTO)
deactivate Peers
Service --> Ctrl : AircraftDTO
deactivate Service
Ctrl --> User : 200 OK (AircraftDTO, status = UNDER_MAINTENANCE)
deactivate Ctrl

alt aircraft is IN_FLIGHT and the target is UNDER_MAINTENANCE / INACTIVE
    R2 --> Peers : 409 {"error": "Aircraft CS-TUC is in flight and cannot change to ..."}
    Peers --> Ctrl : propagated with its status and message
    Ctrl --> User : 409 Conflict
else no replica has the aircraft
    Peers --> Service : Optional.empty
    Service --> Ctrl : EntityNotFoundException
    Ctrl --> User : 404 Not Found
else no peer reachable
    Peers --> Ctrl : RemoteServiceUnavailableException
    Ctrl --> User : 503 Service Unavailable
end

note over User, R3
  Single owner per record: only aircraftmanagement-2 writes CS-TUC, so replicas never conflict.
  When Maintenance calls B3b the same flow runs; a 409/503 is propagated to Maintenance,
  which must not start or complete its record (contract B3b).
end note
@enduml
